@page "/desktop/change-cora-address"

@* The desktop window catches this address before it loads and shows its own connect screen. Anyone who lands here in
   an ordinary browser gets a plain word about it instead of the not-found page. *@
<PageTitle>Change CORA address · Trove</PageTitle>

<h1>Change CORA address</h1>
<section class="trove-card trove-settings">
    <p class="trove-settings-text">
        This is for the Trove desktop window, which keeps its own CORA address. In a browser, Trove comes from whichever
        CORA address you opened, so to use another one, open Trove from there.
    </p>
    <div class="trove-setup-actions">
        <a class="trove-button" href="settings">Back to Settings</a>
    </div>
</section>
